Package: flickos-screenshot
Architecture: all
# python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1,
# gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, gir1.2-pango-1.0: the capture bar and the frozen screen
# (layer-shell surfaces drawn with cairo) and the markup window, GTK 3 so they
# follow the Arc theme.
# grim: takes the pictures. wl-clipboard: every screenshot is copied.
# libnotify-bin: the notification that opens the picture. xdg-user-dirs: the
# Pictures and Videos folders. xdg-utils: a click on the notification opens
# the picture or the recording.
# Recording (docs/design/flickos-screenshot.md, ADR-006): the screen from
# xdg-desktop-portal(-wlr) over PipeWire (gstreamer1.0-pipewire), encoded by
# GStreamer in the same process (gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0): x264enc is in
# plugins-ugly, mp4mux, videocrop and pulsesrc in plugins-good, opusenc and
# audiomixer in plugins-base. wlr-randr: which screen an area is on.
# After a screenshot: sound-theme-freedesktop's shutter sound, played by
# pw-play (pipewire-bin) or paplay (pulseaudio-utils).
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         python3-gi-cairo,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1,
         gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0,
         gir1.2-pango-1.0,
         grim,
         wl-clipboard,
         libnotify-bin,
         xdg-user-dirs,
         xdg-utils,
         xdg-desktop-portal,
         xdg-desktop-portal-wlr,
         gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0,
         gstreamer1.0-pipewire,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly,
         wlr-randr,
         sound-theme-freedesktop,
         pipewire-bin | pulseaudio-utils,
         ${misc:Depends}
# tesseract-ocr: Text, which copies the text in an area or on the screen. It
# is offered only while tesseract is installed (ADR-011): 23.6 MB with its
# English data, too much for every computer (HIG PERF-8).
Suggests: tesseract-ocr
Description: screenshots and screen recordings for the FlickOS desktop
 Take a picture of the whole screen or of an area of it, with a delay if
 wanted, or record a video of it. The area is chosen on a frozen picture
 of the screen, so an open menu or tooltip stays in the shot, with the
 mouse or from the keyboard.
 .
 Every screenshot is saved in Pictures/Screenshots and copied to the
 clipboard, with a shutter sound and a short flash, and a notification
 opens it in a window to draw arrows, boxes and text on it, hide what
 shouldn't be seen, or crop it. Print, Shift+Print and Ctrl+Print
 take one at once; Super+Shift+S opens a small bar with the choices.
 .
 With tesseract-ocr installed, the bar also offers Text: the text in the
 area or on the screen is read and copied to the clipboard.
 .
 Recordings are MP4 files (H.264 with Opus sound) in Videos/Screen
 Recordings. Super+Shift+R starts one, and the panel shows the time and
 stops it.
